{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `yc` and `yb_safestan_flat`. The protected `yb_safestan_flat` represents the original binary observation array `yb` as a deterministic column-major flattening: `yb_safestan_flat[(k - 1) * N + n] = yb[n, k]` for `n = 1..N` and `k = 1..Kb`, matching `to_vector(z)`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `yb_safestan_flat` to the data as a deterministic reshape of `yb`; moved the computation of `z` into the `model` block after `yc` has been observed, because `z` depends on protected `yc`; vectorized the `zb` prior into a single top-level parameter sampling statement; and replaced the looped/indexed binary likelihood with one built-in `bernoulli_logit` statement on the protected flat copy. These are mechanical same-density changes for data satisfying the documented deterministic copy relation.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> K;
  int<lower=0> Kb;
  int<lower=0> Kc;
  array[N, Kb] int<lower=0, upper=1> yb;
  array[N * Kb] int<lower=0, upper=1> yb_safestan_flat;
  array[N] vector[Kc] yc;
}

transformed data {
  matrix[Kc, Kc] I = diag_matrix(rep_vector(1, Kc));
}

parameters {
  array[N] vector[Kb] zb;
  cholesky_factor_corr[K] L_R;  // first continuous, then binary
  vector<lower=0>[Kc] sigma;
  vector[K] mu;
}

model {
  vector[Kc] mu_c;
  vector[Kb] mu_b;
  matrix[N, Kb] z;
  matrix[Kc, Kc] L_inv;

  mu ~ normal(0, 10);
  L_R ~ lkj_corr_cholesky(2);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  zb ~ normal(0, 1);

  mu_c = head(mu, Kc);
  mu_b = tail(mu, Kb);

  yc ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mu_c, diag_pre_multiply(sigma, L_R[1:Kc, 1:Kc]));

  L_inv = mdivide_left_tri_low(diag_pre_multiply(sigma, L_R[1:Kc, 1:Kc]), I);
  for (n in 1:N) {
    vector[Kc] resid = L_inv * (yc[n] - mu_c);
    z[n,] = transpose(mu_b + tail(L_R * append_row(resid, zb[n]), Kb));
  }
  yb_safestan_flat ~ bernoulli_logit(to_vector(z));
}

generated quantities {
  matrix[K, K] R = multiply_lower_tri_self_transpose(L_R);
  vector[K] full_sigma = append_row(sigma, rep_vector(1, Kb));
  matrix[K, K] Sigma = multiply_lower_tri_self_transpose(diag_pre_multiply(full_sigma, L_R));
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":3,"Kb":4,"Kc":3,"N":1,"yb":[[1,0,1,1]],"yb_safestan_flat":[1,0,1,1],"yc":[[2.2188065350077495,2.717056534365478,3.6919197675475934]]}","protected_variables":["yc","yb_safestan_flat"]}
